course: dictionary
lesson: 11656
title: Short forms: ASAP
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: ASAP is a short form called an abbreviation. It stands for «as soon as possible», so it means very soon, without delay.
explain: You will see it in messages, notes and everyday talk, like «Call me ASAP». The word tells the reader that something is urgent and needs doing now, not later.
explain: You can say it as letters, «ay-ess-ay-pee», or as one word, «AY-sap». It is informal, so it suits texts to friends and family, but in school writing use the full phrase «as soon as possible».
fact: ASAP is an abbreviation of «as soon as possible».
fact: It means very soon, without delay.
fact: It is informal, so it is fine in messages but not in formal writing.
fact: In formal writing, write the full phrase «as soon as possible».
fact: ASAP can be said as letters, «ay-ess-ay-pee», or as one word, «AY-sap».
exercise: Mum texted, «Get home ASAP!» What does ASAP mean here? | At a special party | *As soon as possible | As small as a pea | As slowly as you like
exercise: Which words are the full form of ASAP? | at some awful place | as sometimes all people | as safe as prize | *as soon as possible
exercise: Which is best for a formal letter to the headteacher? | *Please reply as soon as possible. | Reply ASAP!!! | Reply asap, thx! | Reply asap lol
test: The coach shouted, «Get your kit on the bus ASAP!» What does ASAP mean? | As safe as a house | Ask someone else | *As soon as possible | As late as possible
test: Which is the correct way to write ASAP in a school essay? | *as soon as possible | Ay-sap for short | Asap | ASAP, just this once
exam: Which sentence means the same as «Call me ASAP»? | Call me whenever you feel like it. | *Call me as soon as possible. | Call me at the end of the week. | Do not call me at all.
